{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "watershed-panel",
  "title": "Watershed Panel",
  "navigationLabel": "Watershed Panel",
  "summary": "Show StreamStats rivers, delineate an upstream basin, and save it as a custom layer or a polygon project.",
  "manualPath": "/user-manual?section=watershed-panel",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-001",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Watershed Panel"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-002",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Open "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Watershed Delineation"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " with the water-waves button in the left sidebar. This panel uses USGS StreamStats to display river channels and compute the upstream basin draining to a selected pour point. Use "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Help"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " (?) to open this chapter or"
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " Tutorial"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " (play) for a guided walkthrough. The tutorial explains the save controls even before a basin is available; it does not delineate or save anything for you."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-003",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1. Choose a state and display rivers"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-004",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Select "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Washington (WA)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Idaho (ID)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", or "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Oregon (OR)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "for the location you want to delineate. Rivers are hidden by default. Check"
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " Show StreamStats rivers"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " to display the selected state’s river channels; uncheck it to hide them. Changing the state updates the river overlay but does not recompute an existing basin."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-005",
      "type": "list",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "For WA and OR, zoom to level "
            },
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "12 or closer"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "; for ID, use "
            },
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "13 or closer"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Look within the selected state. At a wider map view the river layer may be enabled but not visible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Closing and reopening the panel or changing basemaps retains the river visibility setting during the session."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "stepIds": [
        "watershed-panel-005-step-1",
        "watershed-panel-005-step-2",
        "watershed-panel-005-step-3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-006",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "2. Delineate and review a basin"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-007",
      "type": "list",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Zoom to at least level 12, then choose "
            },
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Select point"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". The cursor becomes a crosshair."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Click a river channel in the selected state. A temporary point and a small coordinate popup appear immediately, before the request finishes. The point stays on the map while StreamStats computes the upstream basin; the map does not zoom to a result yet."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "On success, the map draws and zooms to the basin, and moves the same point to the returned StreamStats location when available. Coordinates stay in the map popup rather than a result block in the panel. Click the point to reopen its popup after closing it. The panel shows Basin name and the Save menu."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "ordered": true,
      "stepIds": [
        "watershed-panel-007-step-1",
        "watershed-panel-007-step-2",
        "watershed-panel-007-step-3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-008",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Cancel point selection"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " exits picking mode. During a request,"
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " Cancel"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " cancels the request while keeping the temporary point and popup. A failed or timed-out request also leaves the point available for review or retry; requests may take up to two minutes. Check the state, zoom in, and try closer to a stream channel if no basin is returned. Closing the panel exits picking mode but keeps the point or result and lets an in-progress request finish. Changing basemaps keeps the temporary point."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-009",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "3. Save as custom layer"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-010",
      "type": "list",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Log in and wait until the basin is displayed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Enter a "
            },
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Basin name"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ", open Save, then choose "
            },
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Save as custom layer"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Wait for the confirmation that the layer was saved to "
            },
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Custom Layers / Root"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Open Custom Layers, navigate to Root, and enable the saved layer to show it. You can manage it using the existing custom-layer controls."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "ordered": true,
      "stepIds": [
        "watershed-panel-010-step-1",
        "watershed-panel-010-step-2",
        "watershed-panel-010-step-3",
        "watershed-panel-010-step-4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-011",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This saves the complete basin GeoJSON, including separate polygon parts and interior holes, to your personal layer library. Root is used even if another folder is currently open. The list refreshes after a successful save. If saving fails, the basin remains available so you can retry. Saving a custom layer does not create a project."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-012",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4. Save as polygon for a project"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-013",
      "type": "list",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Log in, open Save and choose "
            },
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Save as polygon"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " after the basin is displayed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "strong",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Edit Polygon"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " opens with the basin boundary already loaded. Adjust its vertices and styling as needed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Save the edited shape to continue to the existing project creation form, with the polygon representation prefilled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "li",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Complete the required project fields and submit the form to save the project."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "ordered": true,
      "stepIds": [
        "watershed-panel-013-step-1",
        "watershed-panel-013-step-2",
        "watershed-panel-013-step-3",
        "watershed-panel-013-step-4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-014",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Opening or cancelling Edit Polygon does not create a project. Separate polygon components are supported. The existing editor does "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "not support interior holes"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ": for a basin with holes, the panel asks you to use "
        },
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Save as custom layer"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " so the complete geometry is preserved."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-015",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "5. Clear results and troubleshoot"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-016",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "strong",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Clear result from map"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is available as soon as a point is placed, including during a request. It cancels any pending request and removes the temporary basin, point and popup. A late response cannot restore a cleared result. It does not hide StreamStats rivers or delete saved layers or projects. Uncheck the river checkbox to hide rivers; manage saved layers and projects in their own panels."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "watershed-panel-017",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If rivers fail to load, check the state and zoom level, then toggle rivers off and on. A service error can prevent the river image from loading even when a network request reports success. If it persists, try again later. River loading errors and basin delineation errors are shown separately. Both save options require login; signing in does not automatically save a basin."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "images": [],
  "examples": []
}
